          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em category of elements
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : \mathcal{C} \to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi el
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} el(F) \to \mathcal{C}
            sitting over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            over an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in \mathcal{C}
            is the set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(c)
          %p
            This is a special case of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+functors"} covariant functors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contravariant+functors"} contravariant functors
            which takes a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:\mathcal{C}^{op} \to \mathrm{Set}
            to a category over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %p
            We may think of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            of “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"}> Set
            \-bundles;” see
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} generalized universal bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is, in this sense, the
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            which is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+opfibration"} discrete opfibration
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Set}
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Set}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+fibrations"} discrete fibrations
          %p
            Forming a category of elements can be thought of as “unpacking” a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            consisting of two objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y
            and two non-trivial morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g
          %p
            %img{:src => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/explode.jpg", :width => "275"}/
          %p
            The individual elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y
            are “unpacked” and become objects of the new category. The “unpacked” morphisms are inherited in the obvious way from morphisms of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %p Note that an “unpacked” category of elements can be “repackaged”.
          %p
            %img{:src => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/implode.jpg", :width => "275"}/
          %p
            The generalization of the category of elements for functors landing in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Set}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Given a functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:\mathcal{C}\to\mathbf{Set}
            %strong category of elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi el
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} el(F)
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi El
                    %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} El_F(\mathcal{C})
            (or obvious variations) may be understood in any of these equivalent ways:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                It is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                whose objects are pairs
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c,x)
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                is an object in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                is an element in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(c)
                and morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c,x)\to(c',x')
                are morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                      %mo :
                      %mi c
                      %mo →
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u:c\to c'
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(u)(x) = x'
            %li
              %p
                It is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                along
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} universal Set-bundle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Set
                        %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U : \mathbf{Set}_* \to \mathbf{Set}
              %p
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
                from
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+set"} pointed sets
                to sets.
            %li
              %p
                It is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (*/F)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
                is the inclusion of the one-point set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo :
                      %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *:*\to \mathbf{Set}
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:\mathcal{C}\to \mathbf{Set}
                is itself:
          %div{:style => "text-align: center"}
            %svg{:height => "89.215pt", :version => "1.2", :viewbox => "0 0 154.323 89.215", :width => "154.323pt", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
